{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{artist: Thomas Chisholm}
{key: D}

[D]Great is Thy faithfulness, [G]O God my [D]Father,
There is no [A]shadow of turning with [D]Thee;
[D]Thou changest not, Thy com[G]passions they [D]fail not,
As Thou hast [A]been Thou for[D]ever wilt be.

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Great is Thy [D]faithfulness, [G]great is Thy [D]faithfulness,
[G]Morning by [D]morning new [Em]mercies I [A]see;
[D]All I have [G]needed Thy [D]hand hath pro[A]vided,
[D]Great is Thy [A]faithfulness, [D]Lord, unto [D]me!
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Summer and [G]winter, and [D]springtime and harvest,
Sun, moon, and [A]stars in their courses a[D]bove,
[D]Join with all [G]nature in [D]manifold witness
To Thy great [A]faithfulness, [D]mercy, and love.
